+## 2026-08-23 — `critic` v0.2.0: fresh adversarial review becomes evidence-bound
+
+`critic` now accepts only a materialized artifact plus its contract. Every surviving finding must
+carry a contract quote, an artifact-relative path/line quote and a counter-argument that survived;
+dead candidates move to `dropped[]`, zero findings require a concrete halt, and the deterministic
+gate rereads every citation. The runtime prompt shrank to the decision surface instead of carrying
+donor history.
+
+TDD caught fabricated quotes, missing contract clauses, silent zero-finding reports and a real
+model failure that retained `survived=false`. Final safe-mode T3 is `8/8` against the strongest
+donor, Codex review-agent, at `2/8`: both find the known defects and keep the clean case clean;
+`critic` adds the sealed ledger/falsification/gate contract. Candidate cost is `13,836` token,
+`29,705 ms`, 0 tools, 0 repeats, consistency `3/3`; donor is `10,198` token, `23,356 ms`.
+
+## 2026-08-23 — `skill-meta` v0.8.0: promotion requires a strongest-donor win
+
+T3 is now one stable three-arm cohort: baseline, strongest applicable donor, candidate. Stable case
+IDs prevent assertion-text reuse across different contexts; donor-passed checks and consistency
+cannot regress, and cost alone cannot count as the strict win. Token, latency, tool, repeat and
+context receipts remain blocking against predeclared candidate limits. The old two-arm tests were
+updated and the isolated T1 check now resolves sibling skill edges without validating unrelated
+suite debt.
+
+RED evidence: old pytest callers failed `5/8`; assertion-only cohort reuse passed; the first fresh
+critic blocked both. GREEN: `8/8` pytest, both eval selfchecks, both isolated T1 checks, and final
+fresh critic PASS. Against `superpowers:writing-skills`, the deterministic gate audit is `8/8`
+versus `2/8`; the external donor still remains the stronger pressure-scenario authoring reference,
+while v0.8 adds Polaris-specific routing, receipts, donor parity and proportional ceremony.
+
